.TH @NP2kai_QT_NAME_UPPER@ 1 "October 2026" "NP2kai" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@NP2kai_QT_NAME@ \- @NP2kai_QT_SUMMARY@
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @NP2kai_QT_NAME@
[
.B \-c
.I file
]
[
.I FD1
[
.I FD2
[
.I FD3
[
.I FD4
]
]
]
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @NP2kai_QT_NAME@
is the Qt 6 frontend of NP2kai, an emulator of the NEC PC-9801 series. It runs under Wayland, where it locks the pointer to the window, and under X11.
.PP
The menu shortcuts work while the mouse is free; once the PC-98 has captured it, every key goes to the PC-98, except Alt+Enter, F11 and F12. Floppy, hard disk and CD-ROM images are changed from the Media menu or the drive icons of the status bar; new images are made with
.B Media > New Floppy Image
and
.BR "Media > New Hard Disk Image" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " file
Read and write the configuration in
.I file
instead of the default one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.I FD1 FD2 FD3 FD4
Insert these floppy disk images in drives 1 to 4, in place of those the configuration remembers.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Left button
Captures the mouse for the PC-98.
.TP
.B Middle button
Captures or releases the mouse.
.TP
.B Alt+Enter
Switches between a window and full screen.
.TP
.B F11
Depending on the F11 key setting: nothing, shows the menu bar in full screen, or switches to full screen.
.TP
.B F12
Depending on the F12 key setting: captures or releases the mouse, or sends a PC-98 key.
.TP
.B Status bar
The loudspeaker button mutes the sound and the arrow button goes back to normal speed; a right click on either shows a slider.
.SH FILES
The configuration directory is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/@NP2kai_QT_NAME@ ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/@NP2kai_QT_NAME@ .
The emulator looks for its ROM images there.
.TP
.I @NP2kai_QT_NAME@.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I bios.rom, itf.rom, sound.rom
BIOS, ITF and sound BIOS ROM images, dumped from a real PC-98.
.TP
.I font.rom, font.bmp
Character font. Without either, it is built from a TrueType font into
.I font.tmp
(delete that file after changing the font).
.TP
.I default.ttf
TrueType font, with Japanese characters, to build the character font from. Without it a few common system fonts are tried.
.TP
.I 2608_bd.wav, 2608_sd.wav, 2608_top.wav, 2608_hh.wav, 2608_tom.wav, 2608_rim.wav
Samples of the YM2608 rhythm part (bass drum, snare drum, cymbal, hi-hat, tom, rim shot).
.TP
.I @NP2kai_QT_NAME@.s00 ... @NP2kai_QT_NAME@.s09
States saved in slots 0 to 9.
.TP
.I @NP2kai_QT_NAME@.s0
State saved on exit and restored on start when Resume is set.
.TP
.I hook_fontrom.txt
Text read from the font ROM while
.B Tools > Text ROM Hook
is on.
